= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions designed in authentic CUET UG single-correct style. The official marking scheme awards $+5$ for each correct answer and deducts $-1$ for every incorrect answer.

#mcq(1, [In traditional security terminology, the policy aimed at preventing war by raising the prospective costs of military attack for an enemy is called:], (
  [Defense], [Deterrence], [Alliance Building], [Balance of Power],
))

#mcq(2, [In which year was the Biological Weapons Convention (BWC), banning the development, production, and stockpiling of biological agents, signed?], (
  [1968], [1972], [1992], [1998],
))

#mcq(3, [The Chemical Weapons Convention (CWC), which banned chemical weapons and mandated their destruction, was opened for signature in Paris in which year?], (
  [1972], [1985], [1992], [2001],
))

#mcq(4, [The Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty (NPT) of 1968 recognized only those states that had manufactured and exploded a nuclear weapon before which cutoff date?], (
  [15 August 1947], [1 January 1967], [18 May 1974], [1 January 1998],
))

#mcq(5, [What is the primary referent object of security under the 'Non-Traditional / Human Security' paradigm?], (
  [The sovereign territorial state], [The military establishment], [Individual human beings and communities], [International alliances],
))

#mcq(6, [The broad conception of human security famously articulated by the United Nations emphasizes which of the following dual ideals?], (
  [Freedom from Arms & Freedom from War], [Freedom from Fear & Freedom from Want], [Freedom of Speech & Freedom of Trade], [Freedom from Hegemony & Freedom from Alliances],
))

#mcq(7, [People who are forced to flee their homes due to armed violence or disaster but remain within the borders of their own country are classified as:], (
  [Refugees], [Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs)], [Economic Migrants], [Stateless Persons],
))

#mcq(8, [Which horrific humanitarian catastrophe in 1994, where 800,000 civilians were killed in 100 days, exposed the failure of traditional security and birthed the R2P doctrine?], (
  [The Gulf War], [The Bosnian Crisis], [The Rwandan Genocide], [The Somali Famine],
))

#mcq(9, [India conducted its first peaceful nuclear explosion experiment at Pokhran (Operation Smiling Buddha) in which month and year?], (
  [October 1962], [May 1974], [May 1998], [July 1999],
))

#mcq(10, [Which of the following is NOT one of the four core components of India's national security strategy?], (
  [Strengthening military capabilities], [Joining formal military alliances like NATO], [Preserving internal unity through democratic accommodation], [Developing the national economy to eradicate poverty],
))

= Detailed Solutions

#solution(1, [Deterrence is the strategic policy of dissuading an adversary from military aggression by convincing them that the expected retaliation and costs will far exceed any potential gains.], answer: [B])

#solution(2, [The Biological Weapons Convention (BWC) was signed in 1972, completely outlawing the development, production, and stockpiling of biological and toxin weapons.], answer: [B])

#solution(3, [The Chemical Weapons Convention (CWC) was adopted in 1992 (opened for signature in Paris in January 1993), banning chemical weapons and establishing the OPCW to oversee destruction.], answer: [C])

#solution(4, [Article IX of the NPT arbitrarily defined a nuclear-weapon state as one which had manufactured and exploded a nuclear device prior to 1 January 1967 (US, USSR, UK, France, China).], answer: [B])

#solution(5, [Unlike traditional security which protects state sovereignty and physical borders, human security makes human individuals and communities the central referent of protection.], answer: [C])

#solution(6, [Human security encompasses both 'Freedom from Fear' (protection from violence and conflict) and 'Freedom from Want' (protection from hunger, disease, and absolute poverty).], answer: [B])

#solution(7, [Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) are displaced by conflict or disasters but do not cross international frontiers, unlike refugees who cross international borders.], answer: [B])

#solution(8, [The 1994 Rwandan Genocide in East Africa resulted in the massacre of nearly 800,000 Tutsis and moderate Hutus, highlighting the failure of traditional UN peacekeeping.], answer: [C])

#solution(9, [India conducted its first nuclear detonation at Pokhran in the Rajasthan desert in May 1974 during the prime ministership of Indira Gandhi.], answer: [B])

#solution(10, [India has consistently maintained a policy of non-alignment, deliberately avoiding joining formal military alliances like NATO or the Warsaw Pact, relying instead on strategic autonomy.], answer: [B])

